  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 325 degrees, cook for 1 and ½ hrs OR 200 degrees for 3 to 4 hrs.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "In a large bowl combine the mushroom soup, celery soup, water, rice, mushrooms, garlic powder and black pepper. Mix all together. Pour mixture into a 9x13 inch baking dish and spread on bottom.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Lay chicken pieces over soup mixture and sprinkle dry onion soup mix over all. Cover tightly with aluminum foil and bake in the preheated oven for 1 and 1/2 hours or until chicken is cooked through and no longer pink inside.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "Brown the chicken before placing it in the baking dish with the rice mixture."
    },
    {
      "text": "I also use garlic/onion powder, seasoning salt and cracked black pepper."
    },
    {
      "text": "It is very important to stir it about every 30 minutes to help the rice cook more evenly so you don't end up with crunchy rice."
    },
    {
      "text": "To top off the chicken, mix plain gluten free bread crumbs with dried basil, a pinch of cayenne pepper, and some more onion soup mix. Make a lot to cover the whole top. To make it crisp up a bit, remove the foil, raise the temperature very high, and cook for a few more minutes"
    },
    {
      "text": "OR top it off with 1/4 tsp of cayenne pepper, a tbsp of dry mustard, and 2 cups of shredded cheddar cheese."
    }
  ],
